# System administrator readiness

**Status: repository prepared; not approved for production launch.**

This file is the operator checklist for a new Vercel/Supabase Free deployment
and a new private GitHub repository. It documents work and checks; it does not
authorize or perform cloud provisioning, migrations, repository creation,
deployment, or a push. Follow [README.md](./README.md) to prepare the new
repository and [db/README.md](./db/README.md) for the exact fresh-database
sequence. Never put credentials in this file.

## Prepared in the repository

- [x] The new repository layout is documented with the application at its
  root and Vercel Root Directory set to `.`. The existing monorepo deployment
  path remains documented separately.
- [x] `vercel.json` defines the Vite build/output, SPA and API rewrites, and
  daily maintenance schedule.
- [x] Fresh Supabase schema bootstrap order, role setup, bootstrap password
  rotation, and the separately executed 007 enum/schema steps are documented
  in `db/README.md`.
- [x] Required server environment variables documented: `DATABASE_URL`,
  `JWT_SECRET`, and `CRON_SECRET`; secrets must be distinct and server-only.
- [x] Supabase PostgreSQL access remains in the API using the restricted
  `ekapon_api` role and transaction pooler; no browser-side Supabase client or
  service-role secret is part of the deployment configuration.
- [x] Local sample/test fixtures are stored outside public assets in the
  excluded `tests/fixtures` directory; the production UI has no fixture link.
- [x] Maintenance cron documentation explicitly says it is cleanup, not a
